WEBVTT

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:14.300
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.680
aoku nemuru mizu no hoshi ni sotto

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.680
Kissing softly the star of water that sleeps in blue,

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:31.410
kuchizuke shite inochi no hi wo tomosu hito yo

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:31.410
A person who lights the fire of life,

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.300
toki to iu kin'iro no sazanami wa

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.300
The time, the golden ripple,

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:45.070
oozora no kuchibiru ni umareta toiki ne

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:45.070
is a sigh from the lips of the sky,

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.300
kokoro ni uzumoreta

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.300
The stars of kindness...

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.270
yasashisa no hoshitachi ga

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.270
...buried in heart flame up...

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.440
honoo age yobiau

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.440
...and call to each other,

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:03.430
namima sasurau nanpasen no you ni

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:03.430
Like wrecked ships wandering on the waves...

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.870
mou nakanaide ima

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.870
Don't cry, any more,

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:16.240
anata wo sagashite iru hito ga iru kara

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:16.240
because now there is a person looking for you,

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.970
omae ni aitai yo to

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.970
Dying to see you...

00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:36.530
Was the meeting between Sarah and Kamille
the mark of an ordinary friendship?

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:39.000
Or were they two Newtypes who resonated
with each other?

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:42.530
Not even these two know for themselves.

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:46.110
Having escaped the explosion in
Von Braun...

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:47.740
...the Argama left the Moon...

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:50.110
...without even the time
to repair its damages.

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:55.120
Unidentified Mobile Suits

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:06.300
I understand what you're saying, but...!

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:08.330
Then we'll proceed straight ahead.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.530
But the Argama's damaged.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:13.540
Are you saying we should return
the Argama to the Moon, Lt. Quattro?

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:14.800
Exactly.

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:16.700
Then I have nothing to discuss with you!

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:18.570
Mr. Wong!

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:23.680
My opinion is also the opinion
of Chairman Melanie Hue Carbine!

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:27.240
If you can't obey him,
I'll have to do something about that!

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:33.360
If we return to the Moon now,
the Titans will make contact with Axis.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:34.860
I know that.

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:38.380
We have no choice but to proceed
as Mr. Wong says.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:42.730
Is it true that Axis is a space fortress
built by remnants of Zeon?

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:43.770
Yes.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:48.600
And not even I have a clue whether
they'll side with the Titans or the A.E.U.G..

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:52.400
It's been a while since I left Axis.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:55.750
How strong a fortress is Axis, anyway?

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:58.780
- Come here, Haro!
- Over here! Over here!

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:01.850
Got you!

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:07.220
- Hey, this is my handkerchief!
- Haro ate it!

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:09.590
- You're lying! You hid it, Shinta!
- I did not!

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:11.890
- Yes, you did!
- No!

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:13.620
Stop it!

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:18.020
<i>Fa is in her element.</i>

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:20.590
Mr. Wong?

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:23.900
Are you done prepping the Gundam,
Newtype?!

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:24.870
No, sir.

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:27.380
Then get your ass to the deck!

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:28.380
Y-Yes, sir!

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:30.650
Ouch!

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:32.910
So, these two are the ones?

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:35.510
The two that Lieutenant Quattro
brought from Earth?

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:36.520
Yes.

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:38.150
What was he thinking?

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:44.120
Do you want some?

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.560
No, I don't.

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:48.720
Children should be more honest
with their feelings.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:51.830
Here, accept it.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:56.630
Go ahead and accept it.

00:03:56.710 --> 00:03:59.510
Okay! Thank you, sir!

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:04.040
Thank you, Mr. Wong.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:17.650
- Aren't you eating?
- Lieutenant Quattro.

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:19.030
I'm not hungry.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:21.660
Would you care for my drink?

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:27.940
I'm sorry.

00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:29.470
No problem.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:30.970
E-Excuse me.

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:42.880
Something seems to be wrong
with Miss Reccoa.

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:46.480
I can't put my finger on it since
I'm always with her.

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:49.620
Have you noticed anything about her,
Lieutenant Quattro?

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:51.220
- Kamille.
- Yes?

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:55.320
For one to delve into another's heart, one
must have the appropriate experience.

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:57.900
I'm well aware of that!

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:01.230
You have that experience,
Lieutenant Quattro!

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:03.030
Do you think so?

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:06.010
It's so easy to grow old
not realizing such things...

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:07.910
...and hurt someone as a result.

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:21.360
How is the Argama proceeding?

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:25.890
It continues to proceed at a low speed
toward the object that left Axis.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:27.590
- Thank you.
- Yes, sir!

00:05:30.170 --> 00:05:33.040
You've met Lieutenant Yazan
of the Alexandria, have you?

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:33.970
Yes, sir.

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:35.830
Tell me what he's like.

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:37.140
Y-Yes.

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:38.700
I'd like to hear your impression.

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:42.430
He's mean and brutal, like a beast.

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:44.280
A beast.

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:46.440
That's accurate.

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:50.280
That's good. Standby for orders.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:51.690
Yes, sir!

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:10.240
The Dogosse Gier is approaching us?

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:12.300
Yes.

00:06:12.710 --> 00:06:14.770
It's sailing exactly parallel to us.

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:16.310
There's no mistake about it.

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:18.510
There seems to be no intention for battle.

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:21.440
Are they trying to beat us there?

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:23.990
What did I tell you?! It's just as I said!

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:28.150
The Titans also intend to make contact
with the people from Axis.

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:32.920
Captain! Attack them at once
before they have a chance to attack us!

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:38.170
We have no information on the Axis ship
we're trying to contact.

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:39.970
At this point...!

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:43.010
We'll wind up in a battle no matter what.
We've got to attack first!

00:06:43.070 --> 00:06:44.410
However...!

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:46.270
How about giving it a try, Captain?

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:47.610
Lieutenant!

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:49.300
Do you have a strategy in mind?

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:51.110
I'll need a little time to get ready.

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:53.980
- How much time?
- Thirty minutes should do.

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:55.950
It'll take you a full thirty minutes?!

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:57.850
You want to crush the enemy, don't you?

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:01.920
Bring in the crew working on the exterior
of the ship!

00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:04.020
We're entering level two battle stations!

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:09.060
We're in a level two battle station!

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:10.100
Lieutenant!

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:12.000
I'm sorry.

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:14.300
I'll head to the briefing room right away.

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:17.000
No, I came because I wanted
a word with you.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:19.410
Lieutenant Quattro.

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:23.210
They're working on upgrading the
Hyaku Shiki's Mega Bazooka Launcher.

00:07:23.450 --> 00:07:24.740
Right.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:30.010
I need a mobile suit to come with
the Hyaku Shiki as its energy tank.

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:32.750
And you want me to pilot it.

00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:34.980
It's a dangerous mission...

00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:37.060
...but I'd like you to do it.

00:07:37.630 --> 00:07:39.220
Sure. I'll do it.

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:41.660
Why are you putting away your plants?

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:46.430
I'm growing sick of their messiness.

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:49.940
Why, I wonder?

00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:53.140
I can't really pinpoint it myself.

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:54.770
Perhaps there's no reason.

00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:58.510
But it's not as if I feel refreshed
by getting rid of them.

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:00.920
What are you suffering from?

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:04.520
- I wonder...!
- Don't you know?

00:08:04.590 --> 00:08:05.560
No.

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:09.250
Is there anyone who truly knows
everything about themselves?

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:11.420
Probably not.

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:12.930
That's why, all I know...

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:17.630
...is that I want to throw everything away
and go away somewhere. That's all.

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:19.470
But you won't be able to.

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:21.900
People are unable to throw away
the baggage they carry...

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:23.130
...until they die.

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:27.070
I understand.

00:08:29.350 --> 00:08:32.180
Do you ever cry, Lieutenant?

00:08:32.850 --> 00:08:35.250
- Sure I do.
- I doubt that.

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:36.290
It's true.

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:50.530
We're attacking in fifteen minutes.

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:52.130
Don't be late.

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:02.270
- I'm going.
- Kamille!

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:05.110
What's he upset about?

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:06.550
Are you sure about this, Ensign?

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:09.140
Not to worry, I'm fine.

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:11.550
Ensign...?

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:14.280
I'm not a child, you know.

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:18.450
The Hyaku Shiki and the Gelgoog,
ready for take-off!

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:21.160
Okay, mobile suit team, take off!

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:26.700
Quattro Bajeena! Hyaku Shiki! Taking off!

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:32.770
Reccoa Londe! Gelgoog! Taking off!

00:09:36.110 --> 00:09:38.240
<i>Sending out the Mega Bazooka!</i>

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:40.150
- <i>Okay, Zeta?!</i>
- <i>Okay.</i>

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:42.680
It's the Zeta! Kamille, go get 'em!

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:46.520
Kamille Bidan... Let's do it!

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:56.460
Shooting out Mega Bazooka Launcher!

00:10:05.740 --> 00:10:07.340
Ensign Reccoa, let's go!

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:09.510
Go ahead!

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:20.020
Can they really destroy the Dogosse Gier
with that thing?

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:22.060
With Lieutenant Quattro handling things,
it'll happen.

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:25.720
How's the Hambrabi, Lieutenant Yazan?

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:29.090
- I don't like it.
- Really? Why's that?

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:31.290
I feel an unfamiliar power.

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:33.700
I don't like the feeling.

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:37.800
The reason you feel that way is because
you've had it easy up to this point.

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:39.170
I've had it easy?!

00:10:39.940 --> 00:10:42.140
Battles cannot be won on strength alone.

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:46.410
You realized the need for more, and
that's why you came to the Dogosse Gier.

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:48.580
Am I right, Lieutenant?

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:52.950
You feel at a loss with the atmosphere
on the Dogosse Gier because...

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:57.390
...this ship is lent an extra power
due to my influence.

00:10:57.460 --> 00:10:59.590
I admire that way
you feel things, Lieutenant.

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:03.930
It gives me a sense of your potential.

00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:09.340
Paptimus Scirocco,
you're an interesting man.

00:11:13.780 --> 00:11:16.580
Enemies! Approaching from
forty degrees starboard!

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:19.640
- How many?!
- Six! No, there could be seven!

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:21.280
Six or seven?!

00:11:21.350 --> 00:11:22.580
Wait, Yazan!

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:25.580
Can you feel it, Sarah?

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:29.190
I think I recognize it.

00:11:29.530 --> 00:11:32.550
- Are they from the Argama?
- I can't be certain.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:36.800
Captain, send out the mobile suits.
I'll leave you in charge.

00:11:36.870 --> 00:11:38.230
- Yes, sir!
- I'm going, too!

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:40.270
Hold on, Lieutenant Yazan.

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:42.970
You should go out only when really needed.

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:47.670
I don't intend to treat you
like the other pilots.

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:50.410
That's good to hear, Scirocco.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:51.780
- I'll be waiting on the deck!
- Right!

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:54.250
<i>Mr. Paptimus and Yazan.</i>

00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:56.290
<i>They've met for the first time, yet...!</i>

00:11:56.350 --> 00:11:58.320
<i>I'm surprised how well</i>
<i>they're getting along.</i>

00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:29.020
The Hyaku Shiki and the Gelgoog
are leaving the formation.

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:30.180
All mobile suits...

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:32.950
...keep a distance from
the Mega Bazooka Launcher's line of fire.

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:34.360
Roger!

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:36.260
- Ensign Reccoa, ready?!
- Yes!

00:12:57.350 --> 00:12:58.780
How many of them are there?!

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:13.760
Send out the second wave!

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:16.630
There aren't too many enemies,
but they've spread out!

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:18.670
Anti-air observers, stay alert!

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:20.100
Well. More or less as I expected.

00:13:26.310 --> 00:13:27.970
Our target is large, but...!

00:13:34.150 --> 00:13:36.620
- Ensign Reccoa, let's do it!
- <i>Yes!</i>

00:13:40.490 --> 00:13:43.590
Energy, at eighty-five percent.

00:13:45.530 --> 00:13:47.360
The problem is, with such a big target...

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:50.400
...one shot isn't going to cause it
fatal damage.

00:13:53.300 --> 00:13:54.860
What?! What's this pressure?

00:13:58.640 --> 00:13:59.840
Paptimus Scirocco!

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:07.380
I missed?

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:09.390
<i>Energy at fifteen percent.</i>

00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:11.390
<i>One minute before we can fire</i>
<i>our next shot!</i>

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:12.820
Three more shots.

00:14:12.890 --> 00:14:14.150
Evasive action!

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:33.570
- We hit it!
- Good!

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:39.880
Lieutenant! Get the Dogosse Gier!

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:41.780
Thanks, Apolly.

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:45.780
Ensign Reccoa, how's our energy?

00:14:46.460 --> 00:14:47.820
Forty percent.

00:14:49.760 --> 00:14:51.590
The Dogosse Gier appears to be damaged.

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:56.300
Way to go, Lieutenant Quattro!
Keep attacking and destroy them now!

00:14:57.300 --> 00:14:59.100
He's way too optimistic.

00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:01.060
Damage on the A-Block deck!

00:15:01.140 --> 00:15:03.940
The weapon used by the enemy
is thought to be an upgraded launcher!

00:15:04.010 --> 00:15:06.070
We have no details on it!

00:15:06.140 --> 00:15:09.200
It's the one they used
when I attacked the Temptation.

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:10.680
I don't like it.

00:15:10.750 --> 00:15:12.110
Mr. Paptimus.

00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:17.550
What do you think, Yazan?

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:19.390
<i>Yeah, I'm going.</i>

00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:20.720
Use your perception in a new way.

00:15:20.790 --> 00:15:23.090
- Can you do it?
- <i>I'll give it a try.</i>

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:25.360
Mr. Paptimus, I'll go, too.

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:27.420
It's okay, Sarah.

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:30.760
You aren't interested in joining
Yazan in the battle, are you?

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:32.770
No, not at this time.

00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:35.270
Then you two would frustrate
each other's feelings.

00:15:35.340 --> 00:15:37.310
Stay behind on this one.

00:15:38.840 --> 00:15:39.900
Hambrabi! Taking off!

00:15:49.190 --> 00:15:51.620
The enemy's got great instincts!

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:53.880
This is going to be fun!

00:15:58.030 --> 00:15:59.960
Ensign Reccoa, thanks for your help.

00:16:00.030 --> 00:16:02.120
- Return to the Argama.
- Right!

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:03.430
Be careful!

00:16:09.870 --> 00:16:11.900
He was saying that Scirocco's there.

00:16:17.050 --> 00:16:20.610
I can sense Scirocco.

00:16:23.090 --> 00:16:25.520
Ensign Reccoa! Where are you going?!
Get back here!

00:16:35.770 --> 00:16:36.990
Thanks, Kamille.

00:16:37.070 --> 00:16:38.930
If you can't fight, return to the Argama.

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:40.130
I'll do that.

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:44.600
What?!

00:16:46.640 --> 00:16:47.940
How dare you!

00:16:56.420 --> 00:16:58.450
I'm amazed you're still alive, Kamille.

00:16:58.520 --> 00:16:59.510
It's you!

00:17:15.210 --> 00:17:17.830
This isn't good! I'm in an awful position!
I'm a sitting duck!

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:22.240
Bastard!

00:17:24.620 --> 00:17:27.080
I guess this Hambrabi is faster than you are!

00:17:32.790 --> 00:17:34.280
Damn it! The vernier's damaged!

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:39.160
I win!

00:17:40.860 --> 00:17:42.130
Out of bullets?!

00:17:48.970 --> 00:17:50.130
What's this?!

00:17:54.910 --> 00:17:56.380
Kamille, are you all right?

00:17:56.480 --> 00:17:57.950
Ensign Reccoa!

00:18:00.650 --> 00:18:02.020
This sensation.

00:18:03.990 --> 00:18:06.920
I feel a pressure unlike any other.

00:18:06.990 --> 00:18:07.720
Who is it?!

00:18:08.260 --> 00:18:10.250
<i>Mr. Paptimus is strong.</i>

00:18:10.330 --> 00:18:13.990
<i>He picked that up in the midst</i>
<i>of all these swirling thoughts.</i>

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:16.130
<i>I'd better get used to this.</i>

00:18:19.340 --> 00:18:22.830
There are ten enemy mobile suits
deployed in the Argama's vicinity.

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:25.870
Don't we have any more mobile suits
of our own?!

00:18:25.940 --> 00:18:27.880
We only have the Methuss!

00:18:27.950 --> 00:18:29.140
Why won't you send it out?!

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:30.610
We have no one to pilot it!

00:18:30.680 --> 00:18:32.270
You have that girl! Fa, was it?!

00:18:32.650 --> 00:18:33.880
No!

00:18:33.950 --> 00:18:36.040
I will never use her as a pilot again.

00:18:38.020 --> 00:18:39.990
Miss Reccoa, please escape!

00:18:40.060 --> 00:18:42.530
Don't worry about me!
At this rate, we'll both be killed!

00:18:42.590 --> 00:18:44.030
I can't leave and let you die!

00:18:44.090 --> 00:18:45.430
Fight, Kamille!

00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:51.490
Miss Reccoa!

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:53.730
Say your prayers!

00:18:58.210 --> 00:18:59.370
Wh-What is it?!

00:19:03.980 --> 00:19:04.950
Kamille!

00:19:05.420 --> 00:19:06.750
What's that?

00:19:17.230 --> 00:19:19.060
What in the world?

00:19:28.940 --> 00:19:30.130
Those mobile suits.

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:37.940
Pull back our mobile suit teams.

00:19:38.020 --> 00:19:40.380
- Dogosse Gier, retreat at top speed!
- Yes, sir!

00:19:44.150 --> 00:19:47.060
So, the luck of the times
has not shifted yet, I see.

00:19:47.320 --> 00:19:48.480
Mr. Paptimus.

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:50.860
How can you be so casual about this?

00:19:51.930 --> 00:19:53.490
Although it's a coincidence...

00:19:53.560 --> 00:19:56.460
...there's always a greater reason behind
an incident like this.

00:19:56.530 --> 00:19:57.470
Y-Yes.

00:19:57.530 --> 00:20:01.400
It could alter the tides of history.

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:04.530
There's no way we can prevail
if we go against such a thing.

00:20:05.510 --> 00:20:08.440
But that's not like you, Mr. Paptimus!

00:20:08.510 --> 00:20:10.740
We'll win in the end.

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:11.780
Captain!

00:20:11.920 --> 00:20:14.750
Tell the mobile suits to retreat at once!

00:20:14.820 --> 00:20:16.220
We'll observe the situation!

00:20:43.850 --> 00:20:47.410
The Zeta Gundam and the Gelgoog
have been retrieved!

00:20:48.450 --> 00:20:49.420
Miss Reccoa!

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:52.450
Miss Reccoa, thank you so much.

00:20:53.760 --> 00:20:56.920
I'm glad I had the opportunity
to return the favor from Jaburo.

00:20:56.990 --> 00:20:59.430
But what were you doing in that area?

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:02.230
The Gelgoog isn't equipped
with any weapons, is it?

00:21:02.300 --> 00:21:05.360
I was able to help you,
so let's leave it at that.

00:21:05.470 --> 00:21:06.700
No, that won't do!

00:21:08.310 --> 00:21:10.400
- Let go!
- Ensign Reccoa!

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:14.740
I need to keep some things
only to myself.

00:21:14.810 --> 00:21:17.080
I don't like you probing into them.

00:21:18.520 --> 00:21:20.240
Reccoa Londe.

00:21:35.700 --> 00:21:38.070
- What's wrong?
- I don't know.

00:21:38.140 --> 00:21:39.100
Kamille!

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:41.830
Were you scolded by Reccoa?

00:21:41.910 --> 00:21:43.130
No, he wasn't!

00:21:51.780 --> 00:21:53.370
I've ended up returning again.

00:22:18.780 --> 00:22:22.730
Is that woman piloting that mobile suit?

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:47.130 --> 00:23:50.590
Char is shaken at the sight
of Haman Karn and Mineva.

00:23:50.830 --> 00:23:53.930
His ensuing actions cause danger
to Kamille and the others.

00:23:54.470 --> 00:23:57.270
On the Argama, running away
from the Gwadan...

00:23:57.340 --> 00:24:00.930
...Char weeps, realizing
the inescapable depth of his own fate.

00:24:01.610 --> 00:24:06.600
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"The Messenger From Axis".

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:12.440
Next Episode

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:12.440
The Messenger From Axis

00:24:07.550 --> 00:24:10.490
You will see the tears of time.
